  "source_pins": [
    {
      "label": "the ten named lifecycles stay ten, and the module says so where a reader meets it. An eleventh mounted lifecycle would be a lifecycle ACC-9 clauses 3-8 never scoped and no pinned test covers",
      "path": "crates/node/src/bin/hypervisor_daemon_routes/m048_collaboration_routes.rs",
      "pattern": "^//! LocalAgentPairingSession, RoomParticipationRequest, RoomParticipantLease, ResourceOffer,$",
      "expect": 1
    },
    {
      "label": "exactly THREE owner-local durable families exist here and they hold no room-child truth: pairing sessions, the terms envelope with its acceptance receipts, and eligibility evidence. A fourth would be owner-local truth the room plane does not own",
      "path": "crates/node/src/bin/hypervisor_daemon_routes/m048_collaboration_routes.rs",
      "pattern": "^    (PAIRING_DIR|TERMS_DIR|TERMS_ACCEPTANCE_DIR|ELIGIBILITY_DIR),$",
      "expect": 4
    },
    {
      "label": "there is NO parallel child registry here: this module never reaches the daemon's generic record store at all, so a room child cannot acquire a second home. Stated as the measured ABSENCE rather than a count of admit-seam call sites, which would move whenever a legitimate one is added and would say nothing about the paths that must stay shut",
      "path": "crates/node/src/bin/hypervisor_daemon_routes/m048_collaboration_routes.rs",
      "pattern": "persist_record\\(|read_record_dir\\(",
      "expect": 0
    },
    {
      "label": "OutcomeRoomDiscovery and ParticipantStateBundle are NOT produced here; both remain M11's, and the unit's scope leaves discovery, portable export, federation, verdict, settlement and acceptance to their declared owners",
      "path": "crates/node/src/bin/hypervisor_daemon_routes/m048_collaboration_routes.rs",
      "pattern": "OutcomeRoomDiscovery and ParticipantStateBundle are NOT produced here",
      "expect": 1
    }
  ],
  "pinned_on": "2026-09-11",
  "rule": "M04.8's unit bar. The predecessor script was `cargo test --locked -p ioi-node --bin hypervisor-daemon m048_collaboration_routes::m048_tests` — a RAW FILTER, which exits 0 when it selects nothing: measured on 2026-09-11, the same command with one character changed reported `test result: ok. 0 passed; 0 failed; 1164 filtered out` and exit 0. Release accounting forbids a check that passes on an empty selection, so every name is pinned — derived from the harness's own `--list`, not from a source regex: the first draft scraped `#[test]` and silently under-derived by 13, because thirteen of these are `#[tokio::test] async fn` and a population that pins only what its regex understood is exactly the fail-empty hole this unit exists to close (the module doc's recorded count of 111 is what caught it), must exist as a `fn` in the pinned source, must be listed EXACTLY by `--list --exact`, and must pass with nothing ignored. The three `m048_*` tests in `outcome_room_system_routes` are pinned as a second family: they prove that a contribution-plane child admits through the room-native seam, which is the runtime half of this population's 'no parallel child registry' source pin, and the predecessor's filter never selected them. NOT claimed: OutcomeRoomDiscovery publication, ParticipantStateBundle production or export, external participation, federation, verdict, settlement and acceptance, all of which this unit's scope leaves to their declared owners, and none of which these tests cover."
